  "reading": "24 of the 36 cells split at least once, so on planted structure the trees are not silent the way they are on the E8 null, and the price of a strict delta shows up as a delay in the first split index rather than as silence. Every cell where both deltas split gives that delay in records: target=value vfdt T=2000 noise=0.2 466.7; target=value vfdt T=2000 noise=0.4 250.0; target=value vfdt T=30000 noise=0.2 1600.0; target=value vfdt T=30000 noise=0.4 600.0; target=value efdt T=2000 noise=0.0 0.0; target=value efdt T=2000 noise=0.2 0.0; target=value efdt T=2000 noise=0.4 0.0; target=group vfdt T=30000 noise=0.0 20800.0; target=group efdt T=2000 noise=0.0 0.0; target=group efdt T=2000 noise=0.2 0.0; target=group efdt T=2000 noise=0.4 0.0. Cells where the strict delta never split inside the stream are recorded with a null first split index and a seeds_that_never_split count, and they are the same statement in a stronger form. The node counts are the other half of the trade, since the loose delta ends with more nodes, which on the E8 null was pure false structure. Both files use the same generator, seeds and deltas, so the null table and this table are two halves of one trade-off and not two experiments.",
